Debug.Assert(Old(_items.Length) == _size);
</code> 
This is because when the array length (capacity) of the ArrayList reaches its limit, it needs to be reallocated and at that point, the size has to be equal to the length again.

<code>
Debug.Assert(RET >= x && RET >= y);
</code> 
This is because the value returned is always greater than or equal to the inputs, x and y.

<code>
Debug.Assert(index == -1 || index >= 2);
</code> 
This is because `index` can either be -1 (which indicates the element is not found) or greater than or equal to 2.

